            "review_text": "Andy M\nHanoi, Vietnam36 contributions\n0\nAshima on Trieu Viet Vuong near Vincom Megamall\nAug 2014 • Couples\nJust had one of the best meals I've had in Hanoi. While waiting for our movies at Vincom, we went to Ashima (Lẩu Nấm Ashima 178 Triệu Việt Vương). Mushrooms are clearly one of their specialties. They had many varieties and served them many different ways. We did not have the hotpot items which were very popular. \n\nThe best nem I've had anyplace by far was the mushroom nem. So yummy! Cooked to perfection. We had a steak and mushroom dish, a lovely salad and a plate of salmon and mushroom sashimi. The service was impeccable. It is not CHEAP... but I don't think it is a poor value. We had all this, three perfect fresh fruit drinks (watermelon and passion fruit) and dessert for less than a million (two people). You could definitely eat for less with the hot pot or simply by ordering less. We were full. I am sure I'll go back!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten August 17, 2014",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
