            "review_title": "Review at Ashima 1",
            "review_text": "DeniseTr\nAtlanta, Georgia78 contributions\n0\nDelicious fun and 'user-friendly' introduction to Hanoi cuisine\nAug 2013 • Friends\nMushroom hotpot and more is available at this upscale Hanoi restaurant. With a dizzying array of mushrooms to choose from, you can create a meal that combines familiar and exotic. The hotpot meal is very sociable, and the vegetarian broth and rich selection makes this a great spot for vegetarians. Though not a vegetarian myself I did not feel I was missing out on anything, as the dinner was fresh and delicious. The décor is glammed up, and you pay for it: with a bottle of wine, the tab came to $25 per person, a little pricey compared to more humble hole-in-the-wall local restaurants. It's in a neat neighborhood that I wish I'd had time to explore.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten September 1, 2013",
