            "review_text": "jimHanoi\nEastsound, Washington141 contributions\n0\nElegant, Exotic, and good for you\nApr 2013 • Friends\nAshima Mushroom Hotpot has three outlets in Hanoi. We have dined at Ashima 2,182 Trieu Viet Vuong near Vincom Center, several times. The setting is upscale and offers excellent service. There are many choices of both cooking stock and ingredients. Many mushrooms are available plus beef, fish, tofu, and black chicken. The servers will help you chose from the man offerings and will help with the cooking. After eating your fill of mushroom varieties, you conclude with vegetables and noodles. They have a nice selection of wines. The restyaurant is very popular with vietmanese and you actually feel healthy eating the various foods but not overfull at the end. It is a wonderful meal for a group and makes a great lunch. Be sure to try to cashews with skin which seem to be a vietnamese specialty.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten April 13, 2013",
